    chapters: [{ number: "01", label: "THE OPENING", title: "A product enters a morning, not a moodboard.", body: "Product in Real Life treats the day-to-day context around an object as part of the launch. The story begins with a routine, a compromise, or an unexpectedly useful moment—not a perfect studio surface." }, { number: "02", label: "THE SYSTEM", title: "Build content around the point of proof.", body: "The client concept identifies the moment a product does something that is easy to understand in real life. It then turns that proof moment into a considered sequence of film, image, useful explanation, and contributor prompt." }, { number: "03", label: "THE CARE", title: "People are witnesses, not raw material.", body: "The system asks for permission, context, and contribution rather than manufacturing testimonials. It describes a respectful content model and makes no claim about campaign reach, sales, or product adoption." }],
