    chapters: [{ number: "01", label: "THE TEXTURE", title: "The routine is richer than the testimonial.", body: "Field Notes begins with a real tension in customer content: polished campaigns often strip out the small circumstances that make a person’s relationship with a product useful and believable." }, { number: "02", label: "THE INVITATION", title: "Ask for a field note, not an endorsement.", body: "The client system invites a person to contribute a routine, a condition, a small observation, or a question with a clear explanation of how it will be used. Context and permission are part of the creative process." }, { number: "03", label: "THE ARCHIVE", title: "Curation can preserve personality.", body: "A designed archive gathers these notes into themes without forcing every contribution into identical brand language. The study is an ethical content model; it makes no claim about beauty-product results or community growth." }],
